# Selected experiments

## E1 fast core versus readout, factorial, on the two sealed valid temporal beds

does the within domain capability come from the recurrent core, from the readout, or from their interaction, on a bed that actually requires temporal order

Separates: H_fast_state, H_readout_capacity, H_bed_insufficiency. Decision information 0.897, cost index 0.28, priority 2.905.

## E4 adaptation locus: state only, head only, adapter only, core, full

can useful fast adaptation occur in owned state without changing shared slow parameters

Separates: H_fast_state, H_interference, H_domain_specific_representation. Decision information 0.73, cost index 0.233, priority 2.783.

## Why this pair

E1 splits the core from the readout on a bed that requires order, which is the only way to tell the fast state hypothesis from the readout capacity hypothesis. E4 splits the locus of adaptation, which is the only way to tell interference from domain specific representation while holding the core fixed. Neither can produce the same verdict under both explanations.

